# Bitvavo.Net Conventions

This rule covers code that uses **Bitvavo.Net** for Bitvavo spot exchange access (no futures, no margin, no testnet), and work on the Bitvavo.Net library itself. Do not write raw `HttpClient` or `ClientWebSocket` calls to Bitvavo endpoints.

## Client setup pattern

```csharp
using Bitvavo.Net;
using Bitvavo.Net.Clients;

using var restClient = new BitvavoRestClient(options =>
    options.ApiCredentials = new BitvavoCredentials(apiKey, apiSecret));
```

Public market data needs no credentials: `new BitvavoRestClient()`.
DI: `services.AddBitvavo()` (namespace `Bitvavo.Net.Extensions`), then inject `IBitvavoRestClient`, `IBitvavoSocketClient`, `IBitvavoSharedApiClient`.
Never hardcode or commit API keys.

## Result pattern

REST methods return `Task<HttpResult<T>>`. Subscriptions return `Task<WebSocketResult<UpdateSubscription>>`.
Always check `.Success` before reading `.Data`:

```csharp
var prices = await restClient.SpotApi.ExchangeData.GetTickerPricesAsync("ETH-EUR");
if (!prices.Success) { Console.WriteLine(prices.Error); return; }
var price = prices.Data.First().Price;
```

`.Error.ErrorType` is the mapped CryptoExchange.Net `ErrorType` (Bitvavo's 90 error codes are mapped). Branch on it, not on message text.

## API surface

- `restClient.SpotApi.{ExchangeData|Account|Trading|Funding|Report|Institutional}`
- `socketClient.SpotApi.ExchangeData` for candle and trade subscriptions
- `socketClient.SpotApi.Account` for the private order and fill stream (authenticated, per market)
- `SpotApi.SharedApi` on REST and socket for `CryptoExchange.Net.SharedApis` (v2). `SpotApi.SharedClient` = legacy v1, same object
- `IBitvavoSharedApiClient`: `GetCapability<T>()`, `GetCapabilities<T>()`, `Discover()` over both transports

## Bitvavo-specific details

- Markets are `BASE-QUOTE`, uppercase, dash: `ETH-EUR`. Same on REST and WebSocket.
- Every order operation needs an operator id (`long`): `BitvavoPlaceOrderRequest(..., OperatorId: 1, ...)`, `CancelOrderAsync(market, operatorId, ...)`, `CancelOrdersAsync(operatorId, ...)`.
- `clientOrderId` must be a UUID: `Guid.NewGuid().ToString()`.
- Only `BitvavoEnvironment.Live` exists. No testnet and no validate-only flag: every order call is live.
- Shared API exchange parameters (exchange name `Bitvavo`): `OperatorId` (`long`), `Markets` (`string[]`, private subscriptions), optional `TriggerReference`.
- Use `KlineInterval` and `BitvavoMarket.TickSize`. `PricePrecision` is null on live markets.
- Error 109 maps to `ErrorType.Timeout`, not transient: read the order back before retrying.
- Rate limiting is one static limiter per process: `BitvavoExchange.RateLimiter` (namespace `Bitvavo.Net.Objects.Internal`). Two budgets of 1000 weight per minute: signed and public.
- `AddBitvavo(o => o.ApiCredentials = ...)` with an untyped lambda configures only the REST client at language version C# 13 or later (the default of net9.0+ projects); at C# 12, the net8.0 default, it picks the library-options overload and both clients get the credentials. Type the parameter, `(BitvavoOptions o) => ...`, or use configuration to configure both clients at every language version.

## WebSocket pattern

```csharp
using var socketClient = new BitvavoSocketClient();
var sub = await socketClient.SpotApi.ExchangeData.SubscribeToTradeUpdatesAsync(
    "ETH-EUR",
    update => Console.WriteLine($"{update.Data.Market} {update.Data.Price}"));
if (!sub.Success) { Console.WriteLine(sub.Error); return; }

await sub.Data.CloseAsync();
```

A subscribe counts as successful once it is sent: Bitvavo sends no per-subscription acknowledgment.
Cancelling the token passed to the subscribe call also closes the subscription.

## Hard rules for consumer code

- Never use raw HTTP or raw sockets for Bitvavo.
- Never use `.Result` or `.Wait()`.
- Never create a client per request in production; reuse clients or use DI.
- Never read `.Data` without checking `.Success`.
- Never omit the operator id on an order operation.
- Never invent method names; inspect `Bitvavo.Net/Interfaces/Clients/**`.
- Not implemented: public ticker and book WebSocket channels, local order book, trackers, multi-user client provider, WebSocket request/response actions, balance subscription, batch orders.

## Hard rules when editing this repository

- TDD: failing test first, confirm RED, then implement. Bug fix = failing repro first.
- 0 warnings and 0 errors on net8.0, net9.0, net10.0. CI builds Release with `-warnaserror`.
- Always braces on `if`, `else`, `for`, `foreach`, `while`.
- No static `*Helper` / `*Util` classes: extension methods (`this T value`) or generics.
- No tuples: a multi-value result is a named `public readonly record struct`.
- XML docs on every public member. English only (code, comments, docs, commit messages).
- Public REST returns `Task<HttpResult<T>>`, subscriptions `Task<WebSocketResult<UpdateSubscription>>`. Never WebCallResult or CallResult.
- Shared API: extend through one partial file per capability + its interface in the aggregate interface + its options in `SetCapabilities`. `BitvavoSharedApiRegistrationTests` fails when the three disagree.
- New REST endpoint = interface member + implementation + a row in `BitvavoEndpointContracts.All`.
- Tests: the only seam is the transport (`StubHttpMessageHandler`, CryptoExchange.Net `TestSocket`, `RecordingSocketFactory`). No mocks of own types. Rate limiting stays on.
- One version number: `<Version>` in `Bitvavo.Net/Bitvavo.Net.csproj`.
- Commands: `dotnet build Bitvavo.Net.slnx`, `dotnet run --project Bitvavo.Net.Tests -f net10.0` (also net8.0, net9.0). `dotnet test` runs 0 tests on SDK 10.

